  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure across the area, will provide mainly dry conditions to \nthe region today. Isolated to scattered showers and storms are \npossible on Sunday, as a shortwave crosses the area, but chances are \nlow enough that it was not included in the forecast per the blend of \nmodels. If it does occur, the bulk of activity is anticipated across \nthe north and east. Better chances for storms are expected early \nnext week, as additional waves cross the area. \n\nThe main story during the period concerns increasing heat and \nhumidity as we progress into next week as upper ridge builds across \nthe area. Temperatures next week will climb into the 90s for much of \nthe lower elevations, and this combined with increasing humidity \nwill result in heat indices in the upper 90s to lower 100s at times. \nHeat headlines may be needed for a period next week.",
